WEBVTT

00:00:01.158 --> 00:00:02.325
[PHOENIX]
My name is Phoenix Wright

00:00:02.408 --> 00:00:03.908
and I'm a defense attorney.

00:00:03.991 --> 00:00:05.616
The Kurain Village's
sacred urn

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:07.325
which holds the soul
of Mystic Ami

00:00:07.408 --> 00:00:10.075
was stolen by the phantom
thief, Mask DeMasque.

00:00:10.158 --> 00:00:12.408
When Ron DeLite
said he was the guilty party

00:00:12.491 --> 00:00:13.991
and surrendered,
I took up his case

00:00:14.075 --> 00:00:16.533
and began investigating,
hoping to uncover the truth

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:18.700
and ensure justice is served.

00:00:18.783 --> 00:00:21.658
However, that didn't
sit right with Maya.

00:00:21.741 --> 00:00:24.950
And thus... I ended up going
into the trial alone.

00:00:26.741 --> 00:00:29.408
[CROWD murmuring]

00:00:35.533 --> 00:00:36.991
What is going on here?

00:00:37.075 --> 00:00:41.116
Why is Mask DeMasque so popular?
He's a criminal.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:42.950
They've even got postcards.

00:00:46.533 --> 00:00:49.158
What are you doing, Nick?

00:00:50.241 --> 00:00:52.200
[PHOENIX]
Maya would love one of those.

00:00:52.283 --> 00:00:55.158
No. I'm on my own today.
Gotta stay focused.

00:02:32.033 --> 00:02:34.700
Court is now in session
for the trial of Ron DeLite.

00:02:34.783 --> 00:02:35.825
Please be seated.

00:02:35.908 --> 00:02:37.241
[RON whimpers]

00:02:37.325 --> 00:02:41.658
Your Honor. The defense
is ready to proceed.

00:02:41.741 --> 00:02:45.658
And what about the prosecution?
Are you ready to begin?

00:02:45.741 --> 00:02:47.033
A foolish question.

00:02:47.116 --> 00:02:48.575
[gasps]

00:02:48.658 --> 00:02:50.950
[GODOT] My caffeinated blood
is always prepared for battle.

00:02:51.033 --> 00:02:54.325
Let's turn the tables,
Your Honor. Tell us--

00:02:54.408 --> 00:02:55.950
Are you ready
to roast this bean?

00:02:56.033 --> 00:02:58.283
[gasps]
Don't be absurd.

00:02:58.366 --> 00:03:00.366
I'll pass judgment after
I've heard both sides

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:01.825
and reviewed the evidence.

00:03:01.908 --> 00:03:03.658
[GODOT] Wake up and
smell the rich aroma

00:03:03.741 --> 00:03:05.908
of a thief admitting his crimes.

00:03:05.991 --> 00:03:09.366
This'll be quick.
We have other cases. Right?

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:11.783
And, um... Who are you again?

00:03:11.866 --> 00:03:16.783
Hmph. Godot. A legendary
prosecutor who's never lost.

00:03:16.866 --> 00:03:20.366
Is that so? And how
many trials have you won?

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:23.575
This'll be the first time
I've argued a case.

00:03:23.658 --> 00:03:25.075
[JUDGE grunts]

00:03:25.158 --> 00:03:26.325
You're a newbie?

00:03:26.408 --> 00:03:28.116
I thought you said
you were legendary.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:31.200
Well, all prosecutors
start off undefeated.

00:03:31.283 --> 00:03:33.491
Be that as it may,
I'd say you're pretty arrogant

00:03:33.575 --> 00:03:34.908
for a rookie.

00:03:34.991 --> 00:03:37.825
Every cup of excellence
begins its life as a mere bean.

00:03:37.908 --> 00:03:39.325
[JUDGE groans]

00:03:39.408 --> 00:03:41.991
[PHOENIX] Why does everyone
I face have to be a nutjob?

00:03:42.075 --> 00:03:45.700
So, we finally meet.
It's a pleasure, Mr. Trite.

00:03:45.783 --> 00:03:47.533
Huh? The name's
Phoenix Wright. And you--

00:03:47.616 --> 00:03:50.450
It is my fate to do
battle with you in this court.

00:03:50.533 --> 00:03:51.991
It's why I've returned.

00:03:52.075 --> 00:03:54.366
I came from the ghastly
depths of Hell to beat you.

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:55.533
[gasps]

00:03:55.616 --> 00:03:57.408
[PHOENIX]
Should I recognize this guy?

00:03:57.491 --> 00:04:00.200
He sounds like he knows me.

00:04:00.283 --> 00:04:01.575
Let's get on with it.

00:04:01.658 --> 00:04:03.908
We'll begin by hearing
from the accused.

00:04:07.366 --> 00:04:08.700
What are you doing?

00:04:08.783 --> 00:04:10.866
We're in the middle
of a trial here.

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:13.741
A brew that's darker
than a moonless night sky.

00:04:13.825 --> 00:04:17.366
Hotter and more acidic
than the devil's bathwater.

00:04:17.450 --> 00:04:20.200
Justice pairs well
with a fine cup of joe.

00:04:20.283 --> 00:04:23.241
[JUDGE gasps]
I suppose I can agree with you.

00:04:23.325 --> 00:04:24.658
[PHOENIX]
Seriously?

00:04:24.741 --> 00:04:28.575
Hello, court. Um, my
legal name is Ron DeLite.

00:04:28.658 --> 00:04:31.200
But, you may know me better
as Mask DeMasque?

00:04:31.283 --> 00:04:32.283
I'm him.

00:04:32.366 --> 00:04:34.325
Wonderful. So,
you admit that you're

00:04:34.408 --> 00:04:37.116
the phantom thief who
stole the Kurain urn, then.

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:38.408
You're telling us the truth?

00:04:38.491 --> 00:04:40.658
[RON]
Yes. I did that crime myself!

00:04:40.741 --> 00:04:42.741
Go ahead and find me guilty.

00:04:42.825 --> 00:04:44.908
Can we please just
get this over with?

00:04:44.991 --> 00:04:46.950
[PHOENIX]
Hold it! One second.

00:04:47.033 --> 00:04:49.033
You're throwing your own case?

00:04:49.116 --> 00:04:51.450
Is there a reason
you're screaming, defense?

00:04:51.533 --> 00:04:52.991
[PHOENIX] Since Ron's
not even trying to say

00:04:53.075 --> 00:04:54.783
he's not the phantom thief,

00:04:54.866 --> 00:04:56.866
all I can do is try to prove
that Mask DeMasque

00:04:56.950 --> 00:04:59.033
didn't actually steal the urn.

00:04:59.116 --> 00:05:01.408
This is nothing
but pure conjecture!

00:05:01.491 --> 00:05:04.241
How do we know Mask DeMasque is
the perpetrator to begin with?

00:05:04.325 --> 00:05:05.700
What's that you say?

00:05:05.783 --> 00:05:08.033
Are you suggesting someone
else broke into the exhibit

00:05:08.116 --> 00:05:10.241
and committed this theft?

00:05:10.325 --> 00:05:12.950
That seems like the first fact
we should get straight.

00:05:13.033 --> 00:05:16.283
Interesting brew.
Let's hear your theory.

00:05:16.366 --> 00:05:19.283
I hope it's as eye opening
as the nectar in this mug.

00:05:19.366 --> 00:05:21.616
Turn your attention
to the screen.

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:23.325
This is security-camera
footage from

00:05:23.408 --> 00:05:25.241
the Lordly Tailor's basement.

00:05:25.325 --> 00:05:26.616
And here.

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:29.908
I have a photo reference
for Mask DeMasque.

00:05:29.991 --> 00:05:31.741
Someone's making
postcards of me?

00:05:31.825 --> 00:05:33.200
[PHOENIX]
Take a close look.

00:05:33.283 --> 00:05:35.533
The thief who broke
into Lordly Tailor

00:05:35.616 --> 00:05:37.658
is missing this gaudy broach!

00:05:38.991 --> 00:05:39.991
It's true.

00:05:40.075 --> 00:05:41.825
Therefore... It stands to reason

00:05:41.908 --> 00:05:44.116
that this criminal is not
the real phantom thief.

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:47.033
[CROWD murmuring]

00:05:49.325 --> 00:05:51.283
Aptly noticed, Mr. Slight.

00:05:51.366 --> 00:05:53.575
But isn't this the broach
you're talking about?

00:05:53.658 --> 00:05:55.283
Hey, where did you get that?

00:05:55.366 --> 00:05:56.825
I found it hidden
at the storeroom,

00:05:56.908 --> 00:05:59.200
in the shadow of a gold statue.

00:05:59.283 --> 00:06:01.741
Wait. It was at the
crime scene all along?

00:06:01.825 --> 00:06:04.866
[JUDGE] Mm-mm-mm... With this
evidence, it would seem it was

00:06:04.950 --> 00:06:08.158
the real Mask DeMasque
who stole the urn after all.

00:06:08.241 --> 00:06:10.158
You're quick on
the uptake, gramps.

00:06:10.241 --> 00:06:11.783
I raise my mug to you.

00:06:11.866 --> 00:06:14.575
[PHOENIX] No! If that was
the real Mask DeMasque,

00:06:14.658 --> 00:06:16.450
then I don't have a case!

00:06:16.533 --> 00:06:19.700
You giving up?
Well, that was easy.

00:06:19.783 --> 00:06:22.408
My coffee hasn't even had
a chance to cool down yet.

00:06:22.491 --> 00:06:23.575
[door creaks]

00:06:23.658 --> 00:06:25.450
Wait just a minute!

00:06:25.533 --> 00:06:27.158
[gasps]
What is it Maya?

00:06:27.241 --> 00:06:28.575
I have a witness.

00:06:28.658 --> 00:06:31.116
He's sitting on something big,
and he can't hold it in.

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:33.908
[PHOENIX]
What? A witness?

00:06:33.991 --> 00:06:35.533
[MAYA]
Mm.

00:06:35.616 --> 00:06:37.241
Yo, Nick, good to see ya.

00:06:37.325 --> 00:06:38.866
Good to see you, Larry.

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:40.366
What are you doing here?

00:06:40.450 --> 00:06:42.950
I saw him. Yesterday.

00:06:43.033 --> 00:06:45.491
Hey, I know you. Butz?

00:06:45.575 --> 00:06:47.908
Oh, whoa. Hi.
What's goin' on, Maya?

00:06:47.991 --> 00:06:50.075
But what could he have
been doing at Ron's place?

00:06:50.158 --> 00:06:52.116
You've got to
hear his testimony.

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:53.741
I promise it'll be worth it.

00:06:53.825 --> 00:06:55.741
[BUTZ]
Have I got a story for you.

00:06:55.825 --> 00:06:57.575
Always here to help, bruh.

00:06:57.658 --> 00:06:59.408
[PHOENIX] Every time I think
I've seen the last of him,

00:06:59.491 --> 00:07:00.950
I have to see more Butz.

00:07:01.033 --> 00:07:04.158
[BUTZ] Look at this. I found it
on my rounds the other day.

00:07:04.241 --> 00:07:06.533
Hey. Is that my wallet?

00:07:06.616 --> 00:07:08.825
[BUTZ]
Hmm. There was a license inside.

00:07:08.908 --> 00:07:11.200
And, you know,
other wallet stuff.

00:07:11.283 --> 00:07:13.200
Anyway, I wanted
to get it back to him,

00:07:13.283 --> 00:07:14.616
like a good citizen.

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:19.491
[PHOENIX] I'm onto you, Butz.
You just wanted to meet her.

00:07:19.575 --> 00:07:20.991
You're skipping
the important part,

00:07:21.075 --> 00:07:22.700
when did you find
the wallet, again?

00:07:22.783 --> 00:07:25.408
Oh, yeah. It was
just two days ago.

00:07:25.491 --> 00:07:27.575
I saw it on the ground
outside my building at work.

00:07:27.658 --> 00:07:29.700
But why would Ron's
wallet be at your job?

00:07:29.783 --> 00:07:31.616
I mean, it's not that weird.

00:07:31.700 --> 00:07:33.700
He works at the
same place I do, right?

00:07:33.783 --> 00:07:34.741
[RON whimpers]

00:07:34.825 --> 00:07:36.075
[PHOENIX]
Really?

00:07:36.158 --> 00:07:38.491
Oh, and I found something
else in his wallet, too.

00:07:38.575 --> 00:07:40.408
A KB Security key card.

00:07:40.491 --> 00:07:43.033
That gets you all over
the building I patrol.

00:07:43.116 --> 00:07:45.283
Each card has
its own serial number.

00:07:45.366 --> 00:07:48.116
We keep logs of when people come
and go throughout the building,

00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:51.200
day and night. That's my
top-notch security for ya.

00:07:51.283 --> 00:07:53.283
He used this? At what time?

00:07:53.366 --> 00:07:56.241
[BUTZ] Let's see. I think
it was around 1 AM.

00:07:56.325 --> 00:07:57.241
[gasps]

00:07:57.325 --> 00:07:59.450
[PHOENIX]
1 AM, two nights ago?

00:07:59.533 --> 00:08:01.200
That's when the urn was stolen!

00:08:01.283 --> 00:08:03.825
Defendant. Is he
correct about the fact

00:08:03.908 --> 00:08:06.325
that you're employed
by KB Security?

00:08:06.408 --> 00:08:10.866
Well, not exactly.
I used to be, until a year ago.

00:08:10.950 --> 00:08:11.950
[PHOENIX]
What happened?

00:08:12.033 --> 00:08:14.533
Um... I was kind of fired.

00:08:14.616 --> 00:08:16.575
Larry. How long would
it take to get from

00:08:16.658 --> 00:08:18.991
your building to Lordly Tailor?

00:08:19.075 --> 00:08:22.450
[BUTZ] Hmm. I'm guessin'.
About 30 minutes or so.

00:08:22.533 --> 00:08:24.200
[PHOENIX grunts]
Half an hour?

00:08:24.283 --> 00:08:25.283
[MAYA grunts]

00:08:25.366 --> 00:08:26.658
That settles it.

00:08:26.741 --> 00:08:28.575
My client couldn't have been
in two different places

00:08:28.658 --> 00:08:30.575
at the exact same time.

00:08:30.658 --> 00:08:32.825
--[gasps]
--And therefore,

00:08:32.908 --> 00:08:35.658
the defendant is not
Mask DeMasque after all!

00:08:39.825 --> 00:08:41.408
Pretty clever, Mr. Blight.

00:08:41.491 --> 00:08:42.741
Color me impressed.

00:08:42.825 --> 00:08:45.408
Although, I'm curious
to know why you went to

00:08:45.491 --> 00:08:48.075
your former place of employment
after you were fired.

00:08:48.158 --> 00:08:49.741
And at such
a late hour, no less.

00:08:49.825 --> 00:08:51.241
[RON whimpers]

00:08:51.325 --> 00:08:52.741
What's going on?

00:08:52.825 --> 00:08:54.325
Look at this, Nick!

00:08:56.325 --> 00:08:57.908
A letter?

00:08:57.991 --> 00:09:00.116
[MAYA]
I found it at Ron's place.

00:09:01.408 --> 00:09:02.991
Is this what I think it is?

00:09:03.075 --> 00:09:05.283
I remembered what
Desiree said earlier.

00:09:05.366 --> 00:09:07.116
There's a lot more to
this case than meets the eye!

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:09.491
I know it! Please!

00:09:09.575 --> 00:09:11.158
I'm begging you!

00:09:11.241 --> 00:09:13.033
She wasn't exaggerating.

00:09:13.116 --> 00:09:15.533
I think this note could be
what she was talking about.

00:09:15.616 --> 00:09:17.616
[gasps]
That's great!

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:20.408
I'm really sorry about
what happened yesterday.

00:09:20.491 --> 00:09:22.658
You two ended up
fighting because of me.

00:09:22.741 --> 00:09:25.325
Don't say that!
I was the one who was wrong.

00:09:25.408 --> 00:09:28.616
You both have
my gratitude. Thanks alot.

00:09:29.825 --> 00:09:31.866
[PHOENIX] Your Honor!
The defense would now like to

00:09:31.950 --> 00:09:33.908
present a shocking
new piece of evidence!

00:09:33.991 --> 00:09:36.200
[gasps]
No, please, not that!

00:09:37.991 --> 00:09:40.116
[PHOENIX]
"Bring me 50,000 dollars."

00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:42.533
Your Honor, this is
obviously blackmail.

00:09:42.616 --> 00:09:44.991
While the theft was taking place
on the other side of town,

00:09:45.075 --> 00:09:47.700
Ron DeLite was dealing with
whoever wrote this letter...

00:09:47.783 --> 00:09:50.825
...in the CEO's
office at KB security!

00:09:50.908 --> 00:09:53.408
Fascinating. But do you
have concrete proof

00:09:53.491 --> 00:09:56.616
that the kid even entered
the CEO's office?

00:09:56.700 --> 00:09:57.950
Well. I'm sure that we--

00:09:58.033 --> 00:10:00.075
Of course we've got proof.

00:10:00.158 --> 00:10:01.741
C'mon, tell 'em, Larry.

00:10:01.825 --> 00:10:04.700
Sure thang. Look up the
logs connected to the key card,

00:10:04.783 --> 00:10:06.616
and they'll tell you exactly
what doors he went through

00:10:06.700 --> 00:10:07.658
and at what time.

00:10:07.741 --> 00:10:09.700
You can do that?

00:10:09.783 --> 00:10:11.158
[BUTZ chuckles]

00:10:11.241 --> 00:10:14.241
[JUDGE] Prosecutor Godot.
Do you approve?

00:10:14.325 --> 00:10:16.991
Sure. In fact, I have them here.

00:10:17.075 --> 00:10:20.033
These are the card logs
for the CEO's office.

00:10:20.116 --> 00:10:23.408
There is a record for 1 AM the
night the crime was committed.

00:10:23.491 --> 00:10:25.783
And I'm guessing
it was DeLite's card.

00:10:25.866 --> 00:10:27.408
What? You knew about this?

00:10:27.491 --> 00:10:28.991
I don't understand.

00:10:29.075 --> 00:10:31.783
Heh. I'm meticulous
with my ground work,

00:10:31.866 --> 00:10:33.741
with both research and coffee.

00:10:33.825 --> 00:10:36.783
[PHOENIX] Was he testing me?
Or is something else going on.

00:10:36.866 --> 00:10:38.366
[GODOT]
Quote, "If you don't want

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:41.783
your secret identity
revealed." End quote.

00:10:41.866 --> 00:10:43.866
I wonder what
all this could be about.

00:10:43.950 --> 00:10:47.033
See! He's talking about
the fact I'm Mask DeMasque.

00:10:47.116 --> 00:10:48.200
[gasps]

00:10:48.283 --> 00:10:49.991
Irrelevant! The defendant
clearly wasn't

00:10:50.075 --> 00:10:52.450
the person who stole
the urn that night.

00:10:52.533 --> 00:10:53.866
I must agree with you.

00:10:53.950 --> 00:10:56.491
DeLite was in the CEO's
office at KB Security

00:10:56.575 --> 00:10:58.241
when the crime took place.

00:10:58.325 --> 00:11:00.241
The prosecutor's office
will admit that this fact

00:11:00.325 --> 00:11:02.491
should be on the record.

00:11:02.575 --> 00:11:05.450
--[gasps]
--You did it! He's not guilty.

00:11:05.533 --> 00:11:07.866
--Thank you.
--This isn't right.

00:11:07.950 --> 00:11:10.408
I am the phantom thief,
I swear it's true.

00:11:10.491 --> 00:11:12.533
Well, if the defendant
didn't do it.

00:11:12.616 --> 00:11:15.200
Then who's the
guilty party responsible?

00:11:15.283 --> 00:11:17.033
We're now without a suspect.

00:11:17.116 --> 00:11:19.700
[PHOENIX] Whoever stole the urn
must have been in the warehouse.

00:11:19.783 --> 00:11:22.283
It's the only thing
that makes sense.

00:11:22.366 --> 00:11:24.241
But who was there at the time?

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:29.200
[PHOENIX]
Don't tell me!

00:11:29.283 --> 00:11:30.408
Heh.

00:11:30.491 --> 00:11:32.991
I believe I know who
the thief may have been.

00:11:33.075 --> 00:11:35.200
Oh, yeah? Do tell us.

00:11:35.283 --> 00:11:38.700
The culprit--
is the prosecutor's witness.

00:11:38.783 --> 00:11:42.116
The real Mask DeMasque is
Ace Detective Luke Atmey!

00:11:47.575 --> 00:11:49.533
[LUKE]
Greetings, ladies and gentlemen!

00:11:49.616 --> 00:11:50.950
I have arrived.

00:11:52.491 --> 00:11:55.616
[JUDGE] Now then, witness.
State your name and occupation.

00:11:55.700 --> 00:11:58.116
You've no doubt
heard of Luke Atmey.

00:11:58.200 --> 00:12:00.116
Ace Detective and
stunning star skilled

00:12:00.200 --> 00:12:01.533
at stealing the spotlight.

00:12:01.616 --> 00:12:03.491
Would you mind using
some of that illumination

00:12:03.575 --> 00:12:05.408
to lighten the dark
roast in my cup?

00:12:05.491 --> 00:12:08.158
But of course.
Your wish is my command.

00:12:08.241 --> 00:12:10.575
We've got two
real pieces of work here.

00:12:10.658 --> 00:12:12.908
It's like they're feeding
on each others' weirdness.

00:12:12.991 --> 00:12:13.908
Just my luck.

00:12:13.991 --> 00:12:16.116
This is simply unbelievable.

00:12:16.200 --> 00:12:18.991
You seek to indict me,
the Duke of Deduction?

00:12:19.075 --> 00:12:21.158
It seems as though you've
chosen to ignore the rules

00:12:21.241 --> 00:12:23.950
of civil society again.

00:12:24.033 --> 00:12:25.200
Are you sure you're
going to be able to

00:12:25.283 --> 00:12:27.241
win this one, Mr. Nick?

00:12:27.325 --> 00:12:29.825
I've got no choice
but to try my best.

00:12:29.908 --> 00:12:32.658
First off, Mr. Atmey...

00:12:33.658 --> 00:12:35.950
Remember what
you said yesterday?

00:12:36.033 --> 00:12:38.741
[LUKE] Indeed! And since
I am an Ace Detective,

00:12:38.825 --> 00:12:41.866
I expertly arranged an elegant
trap to ensnare the thief.

00:12:41.950 --> 00:12:44.366
In other words, it was
possible for you to easily

00:12:44.450 --> 00:12:45.866
steal the Kurain urn.

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:48.366
Wait. So, the
detective is the thief?

00:12:48.450 --> 00:12:51.325
Sadly for you, Sir Lawyer,
that vibrant picture

00:12:51.408 --> 00:12:53.491
of the villain behind you
speaks louder than a wealth

00:12:53.575 --> 00:12:55.075
of worthless words.

00:12:55.158 --> 00:12:57.241
As you can see,
it points to Mask DeMasque

00:12:57.325 --> 00:12:59.075
as the culprit, not me!

00:13:00.283 --> 00:13:02.033
By the way, that
footage was captured

00:13:02.116 --> 00:13:04.241
by a Lordly Tailor camera, yes?

00:13:04.325 --> 00:13:05.950
So, it hasn't
been tampered with.

00:13:07.200 --> 00:13:09.158
Because there
was no need for it to be.

00:13:09.241 --> 00:13:10.533
[LUKE whimpers]

00:13:10.616 --> 00:13:12.450
You could pretend to be
on guard duty as a detective

00:13:12.533 --> 00:13:15.366
and also steal the urn
as a phantom thief!

00:13:15.450 --> 00:13:18.741
Luke Atmey!
You are Mask DeMasque.

00:13:18.825 --> 00:13:19.908
Admit it!

00:13:19.991 --> 00:13:21.491
[yelped]

00:13:21.575 --> 00:13:23.700
What say you
to this charge, witness?

00:13:26.658 --> 00:13:28.033
[cackles]

00:13:28.116 --> 00:13:29.450
He's laughing?

00:13:31.866 --> 00:13:35.283
Yes, Mask DeMasque is
truly a maniacal mastermind.

00:13:35.366 --> 00:13:37.283
And as such, I,
Detective Luke Atmey,

00:13:37.366 --> 00:13:39.866
am the only genuine genius
with the deftness and daring

00:13:39.950 --> 00:13:42.241
to don the dastardly disguise.

00:13:42.325 --> 00:13:43.616
Wouldn't you agree?

00:13:43.700 --> 00:13:45.991
Are you admitting that
you're guilty of this crime?

00:13:46.075 --> 00:13:47.408
You've got 'em!

00:13:48.366 --> 00:13:50.033
Yes, Mr. Atmey!

00:13:50.116 --> 00:13:52.283
I hereby indict you
as Mask DeMasque.

00:13:52.366 --> 00:13:54.241
[GODOT]
Objection!

00:13:54.325 --> 00:13:55.241
[gasping]

00:13:55.325 --> 00:13:57.033
[PHOENIX gaqsps]

00:13:57.116 --> 00:13:59.450
[GODOT]
Godot Blend number 102.

00:13:59.533 --> 00:14:00.950
Have a sample on the house.

00:14:01.033 --> 00:14:02.658
Sir. What's the meaning of this?

00:14:02.741 --> 00:14:05.241
The Detective is
really an Ace Thief?

00:14:05.325 --> 00:14:07.908
It's a fairy tale filled with
sweetener to be sure,

00:14:07.991 --> 00:14:10.200
but reality is far more bitter.

00:14:11.575 --> 00:14:13.325
I have to admit,
his theory makes

00:14:13.408 --> 00:14:14.825
perfect sense to me.

00:14:14.908 --> 00:14:18.033
It would make sense
if there were any truth to it,

00:14:18.116 --> 00:14:19.366
Mr. Smite.

00:14:19.450 --> 00:14:20.408
[PHOENIX groans]

00:14:20.491 --> 00:14:22.616
The Urn's guardian is its thief?

00:14:22.700 --> 00:14:24.366
That's quite the narrative.

00:14:24.450 --> 00:14:27.283
But you'd better show all of us
the proof of your claim.

00:14:27.366 --> 00:14:29.408
Otherwise, I suggest that
you throw out the pot

00:14:29.491 --> 00:14:30.908
and try another grind.

00:14:30.991 --> 00:14:32.241
Yes, indeed.

00:14:32.325 --> 00:14:34.658
You're rambling randomly
in an attempt to revile me

00:14:34.741 --> 00:14:36.491
as a rapscallion, right?

00:14:36.575 --> 00:14:39.116
I can't imagine
you have any evidence.

00:14:39.200 --> 00:14:41.116
[PHOENIX sighs]

00:14:41.200 --> 00:14:42.283
[PHOENIX]
I'd love to settle things

00:14:42.366 --> 00:14:44.741
right here and now, but...

00:14:44.825 --> 00:14:46.575
[JUDGE]
Defense?

00:14:46.658 --> 00:14:49.283
Your Honor.
I don't have proof yet...

00:14:49.366 --> 00:14:50.616
[gasps]

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:53.450
[GODOT] Hmm. As I thought.
The brew has gone stale,

00:14:53.533 --> 00:14:55.741
but you're trying to
force it down anyway.

00:14:55.825 --> 00:14:58.658
[PHOENIX] This is no good!
I've got to stay on the attack!

00:14:58.741 --> 00:15:01.033
I'll never get another chance
to prove he's the thief!

00:15:01.116 --> 00:15:03.866
[LUKE] Hmm. Sounds like you
can't back up your claims.

00:15:03.950 --> 00:15:05.033
[PHOENIX whimpers]

00:15:05.116 --> 00:15:06.908
It seems the cloud
of suspicion surrounding

00:15:06.991 --> 00:15:09.116
this witness has lifted,
and therefore we--

00:15:09.200 --> 00:15:10.658
[DESIRÉE]
Hold it!

00:15:10.741 --> 00:15:11.658
[JUDGE gasps]

00:15:11.741 --> 00:15:12.700
[gasping]

00:15:14.866 --> 00:15:15.908
--Dessie, dear!
--Desiree!

00:15:15.991 --> 00:15:18.116
Look at this. Tah-dah!

00:15:18.200 --> 00:15:19.116
[gasping]

00:15:19.200 --> 00:15:20.825
Wait. Is that the...

00:15:20.908 --> 00:15:24.075
[MAYA gasps]
The Kurain urn!

00:15:24.158 --> 00:15:25.575
But where did you find it?

00:15:25.658 --> 00:15:26.950
Isn't that obvious?

00:15:27.033 --> 00:15:29.033
It was in this shady
detective's office!

00:15:30.908 --> 00:15:33.658
Detective Atmey's office.
Does that mean...

00:15:34.908 --> 00:15:36.408
I wanted to help
Ronnie get out of this

00:15:36.491 --> 00:15:37.450
any way I could.

00:15:37.533 --> 00:15:38.700
[RON whimpers]

00:15:38.783 --> 00:15:42.575
Ahh... Isn't the power
of love so beautiful?

00:15:42.658 --> 00:15:44.158
No. That can't be...

00:15:44.241 --> 00:15:46.241
You'll find it hard to
weasel out of this one!

00:15:46.325 --> 00:15:48.533
The evidence points to guilty!

00:15:48.616 --> 00:15:51.783
[GODOT] Objection!
You're jumping to conclusions.

00:15:51.866 --> 00:15:53.200
Desirée.

00:15:53.283 --> 00:15:55.783
You're Ron DeLite's loving
wife, is that correct?

00:15:55.866 --> 00:15:57.283
[DESIRÉE]
Yes, of course I am.

00:15:57.366 --> 00:15:59.158
I have to commend you.

00:15:59.241 --> 00:16:01.033
The lengths you've gone
to save your husband

00:16:01.116 --> 00:16:02.866
are truly inspiring.

00:16:02.950 --> 00:16:04.616
What do you mean by that?

00:16:04.700 --> 00:16:06.408
It'd be the easiest
thing in the world for you

00:16:06.491 --> 00:16:10.241
to bring the urn to us, from the
home you share with Ron.

00:16:10.325 --> 00:16:11.408
[CROWD gasping]

00:16:11.491 --> 00:16:14.908
That's not true!
I found it in his office!

00:16:14.991 --> 00:16:16.533
The scalding truth is...

00:16:16.616 --> 00:16:18.908
...this town is filled
to the brim with lies.

00:16:18.991 --> 00:16:21.408
We don't need any more
getting through the filter.

00:16:21.491 --> 00:16:23.450
[DESIRÉE]
You're wrong! I would never.

00:16:23.533 --> 00:16:26.241
[JUDGE]
I see his point.

00:16:26.325 --> 00:16:29.075
If you cannot prove that the urn
was in the witness's office,

00:16:29.158 --> 00:16:32.658
I simply cannot accept it
as evidence in this court!

00:16:32.741 --> 00:16:34.408
Don't forget
to tip your barista.

00:16:34.491 --> 00:16:35.825
[PHOENIX]
Objection!

00:16:39.325 --> 00:16:41.200
[GODOT gasps]

00:16:41.283 --> 00:16:44.741
The urn was in fact
in Detective Atmey's office,

00:16:44.825 --> 00:16:47.033
and I can prove that to be true.

00:16:47.116 --> 00:16:49.200
Because of the
fingerprints on it!

00:16:50.408 --> 00:16:52.116
[GODOT]
Fingerprints? Really?

00:16:52.200 --> 00:16:55.491
Oh, dear. Don't make
us laugh, Sir Lawyer.

00:16:55.575 --> 00:16:57.825
That's your big reveal? My, my.

00:16:57.908 --> 00:16:59.325
How thickheaded.

00:16:59.408 --> 00:17:01.825
It would be perfectly plausible
if that urn was plastered

00:17:01.908 --> 00:17:03.533
in my fingerprints.

00:17:03.616 --> 00:17:05.575
After all, I was
the slick sentinel

00:17:05.658 --> 00:17:07.366
assigned its safety.

00:17:07.450 --> 00:17:09.450
[PHOENIX]
Hmph. Unfortunately for you,

00:17:09.533 --> 00:17:11.908
I'm not presenting your
fingerprints as evidence.

00:17:11.991 --> 00:17:12.908
[gasps]

00:17:12.991 --> 00:17:14.075
Mr. Atmey.

00:17:14.158 --> 00:17:17.366
Do you recall when
you saw me yesterday?

00:17:17.450 --> 00:17:20.616
The Kurain urn was
in your bag then, wasn't it?

00:17:20.700 --> 00:17:22.116
That's quite impossible.

00:17:22.200 --> 00:17:24.700
Sure, I didn't look
in the bag myself.

00:17:24.783 --> 00:17:28.491
But even better than that.
I touched whatever was inside!

00:17:28.575 --> 00:17:30.366
What! You did?

00:17:30.450 --> 00:17:31.575
[PHOENIX]
Your Honor!

00:17:31.658 --> 00:17:33.741
Please have the urn
dusted for fingerprints.

00:17:33.825 --> 00:17:35.991
If my prints are on there,
it proves beyond a doubt

00:17:36.075 --> 00:17:38.991
that the urn was in Detective
Atmey's office after all!

00:17:39.075 --> 00:17:42.450
[GODOT] Objection! Isn't it
possible you could have touched

00:17:42.533 --> 00:17:44.575
the urn sometime
before it was stolen?

00:17:44.658 --> 00:17:46.116
It's not.

00:17:46.200 --> 00:17:49.408
As the person in charge of the
exhibition explained to us.

00:17:49.491 --> 00:17:51.366
But I did my best to
polish it and make it look

00:17:51.450 --> 00:17:52.783
like it was worth millions!

00:17:52.866 --> 00:17:55.158
I think it's quite a beautiful
work of art, honestly!

00:17:55.241 --> 00:17:57.575
She must've removed
every fingerprint.

00:17:57.658 --> 00:18:01.158
So, the only chance I had to
touch the urn was yesterday.

00:18:01.241 --> 00:18:02.366
And that's...

00:18:02.450 --> 00:18:05.325
...when I was at
the Atmey Detective Agency!

00:18:05.408 --> 00:18:07.450
[LUKE whimpers]

00:18:07.533 --> 00:18:11.325
Heh. That's the Godot
Blend number 107.

00:18:11.408 --> 00:18:14.408
Suddenly, it seems way
too bitter for my taste.

00:18:14.491 --> 00:18:15.491
[CROWD murmuring]

00:18:15.575 --> 00:18:17.908
Officer! Take
this urn and examine--

00:18:17.991 --> 00:18:20.950
[LUKE] There's no need
for such a display.

00:18:21.033 --> 00:18:23.533
That's because... I already
know the pompous

00:18:23.616 --> 00:18:25.658
prosecutor's prints
polluted the piece.

00:18:25.741 --> 00:18:27.658
[gasps]
What are you saying?

00:18:27.741 --> 00:18:29.908
[PHOENIX]
This is it. I finally broke him.

00:18:29.991 --> 00:18:34.533
[LUKE cackles]

00:18:34.616 --> 00:18:35.783
Take a good long look,

00:18:35.866 --> 00:18:37.575
ladies and gentlemen
of the court!

00:18:37.658 --> 00:18:39.991
You may think it vain,
but to find a proper rival,

00:18:40.075 --> 00:18:42.575
I was forced to create
my own villainous virtuoso.

00:18:42.658 --> 00:18:44.408
A vengeful vigilante.

00:18:44.491 --> 00:18:46.700
Your acute accusations
are all affirmed.

00:18:46.783 --> 00:18:49.866
It was me! I am the one
and only Mask DeMasque!

00:18:49.950 --> 00:18:53.908
I hope you all enjoyed
my perfectly poised performance!

00:18:53.991 --> 00:18:58.575
[cackles]

00:18:59.950 --> 00:19:02.450
[JUDGE]
Well. Prosecutor Godot.

00:19:02.533 --> 00:19:04.158
What's Atmey's current status?

00:19:04.241 --> 00:19:06.741
[GODOT] He's still in the lobby,
laughing like a madman.

00:19:06.825 --> 00:19:09.491
I wish I could laugh
like that, to be honest.

00:19:11.491 --> 00:19:13.825
That being said, I shall
hereby hand down the verdict

00:19:13.908 --> 00:19:16.450
in the case against Ron DeLite!

00:19:16.533 --> 00:19:17.616
Not guilty!

00:19:17.700 --> 00:19:19.825
[CROWD cheering]

00:19:20.866 --> 00:19:23.033
[DESIRÉE]
Nicky boy! Thank you so much.

00:19:23.116 --> 00:19:25.408
For everything. You're a genius.

00:19:25.491 --> 00:19:28.075
No. I couldn't have
done it without your help.

00:19:28.158 --> 00:19:30.991
Talk about a thrill.
She really turned the tide.

00:19:31.075 --> 00:19:33.575
I wanna be just
like her when I grow up.

00:19:33.658 --> 00:19:34.825
And Maya and Pearl,

00:19:34.908 --> 00:19:36.908
I really have to thank
the both of you, too.

00:19:36.991 --> 00:19:38.491
You helped so much.

00:19:38.575 --> 00:19:40.575
I'm glad we were able to!

00:19:42.283 --> 00:19:43.700
What's the matter?

00:19:43.783 --> 00:19:46.700
I did my best to get you out of
this, so why are you down?

00:19:46.783 --> 00:19:49.283
You're right. I know.

00:19:49.366 --> 00:19:52.200
And I really appreciate it,
honey. The thing is--

00:19:52.283 --> 00:19:54.783
[GODOT] It's a little
too early to celebrate.

00:19:55.825 --> 00:19:57.700
[PHOENIX]
Godot! What are you doing here?

00:19:57.783 --> 00:20:00.658
I just came to give
my thanks for your assistance.

00:20:00.741 --> 00:20:02.158
[MAYA]
For what, now?

00:20:02.241 --> 00:20:03.658
On another case.

00:20:03.741 --> 00:20:04.991
Early this morning, the body

00:20:05.075 --> 00:20:08.866
of KB Security's CEO Kane
Bullard was discovered.

00:20:08.950 --> 00:20:10.283
[gasping]

00:20:10.366 --> 00:20:13.783
He had been murdered,
and the estimated time of death

00:20:13.866 --> 00:20:16.700
is 1 AM on September 12th.

00:20:16.783 --> 00:20:18.991
[PHOENIX]
1 AM? You don't mean...

00:20:19.075 --> 00:20:20.491
That's right,
at the same time

00:20:20.575 --> 00:20:22.658
a cheap little art piece
was being stolen,

00:20:22.741 --> 00:20:25.658
there was a murder
happening over at KB Security.

00:20:25.741 --> 00:20:28.491
All right, then.
What brings you here?

00:20:28.575 --> 00:20:30.866
We work well together
and proved a few things

00:20:30.950 --> 00:20:33.616
in court today. On the record.

00:20:33.700 --> 00:20:34.950
[PHOENIX]
Like what?

00:20:35.033 --> 00:20:38.325
Like the fact that on
September 12th at 1 AM,

00:20:38.408 --> 00:20:42.866
one Mr. Ron DeLite was in the
office of KB Security's CEO.

00:20:42.950 --> 00:20:45.450
The scene of the murder.

00:20:45.533 --> 00:20:47.325
After getting
that blackmail letter,

00:20:47.408 --> 00:20:50.575
he must've been
imbrued with utter rage.

00:20:50.658 --> 00:20:51.575
[gasps]

00:20:51.658 --> 00:20:52.950
[GODOT]
That's right.

00:20:53.033 --> 00:20:55.741
We proved the kid's
whereabouts in today's trial.

00:20:55.825 --> 00:20:57.700
It may have been his alibi,

00:20:57.783 --> 00:20:59.991
but it implicated him
in a more serious crime.

00:21:00.075 --> 00:21:01.200
Oh, no.

00:21:01.283 --> 00:21:03.783
The defendant didn't
steal the urn, true.

00:21:03.866 --> 00:21:05.700
Because he was
murdering Kane Bullard

00:21:05.783 --> 00:21:06.991
at the time of the theft.

00:21:07.075 --> 00:21:08.033
[gasps]

00:21:08.116 --> 00:21:09.866
No! I don't believe it!

00:21:09.950 --> 00:21:11.241
I'm innocent.

00:21:11.325 --> 00:21:14.033
I'm only a thief, I swear.
I'd never hurt anybody,

00:21:14.116 --> 00:21:15.408
not even a fly.

00:21:15.491 --> 00:21:18.200
We'll have to detain
you for a little while longer.

00:21:18.283 --> 00:21:20.741
On a different charge this time.

00:21:20.825 --> 00:21:22.283
[GODOT]
You're going down for murder.

00:21:22.366 --> 00:21:25.741
What do we do? There's
no way that Ron's a killer.

00:21:25.825 --> 00:21:28.241
Was this your goal from
the very beginning, Godot?

00:21:28.325 --> 00:21:30.825
We're in for another showdown.

00:21:30.908 --> 00:21:32.741
I'm buzzing with excitement.

00:21:32.825 --> 00:21:34.408
[PHOENIX]
Just who is this guy?

00:21:34.491 --> 00:21:37.491
I sense a quiet but deep
hatred coming from him!

00:21:37.575 --> 00:21:39.533
What's he getting out of this?

00:21:39.616 --> 00:21:42.075
No! Ronnie!

00:21:43.491 --> 00:21:46.825
[PHOENIX]
Ron DeLite? A murderer?

00:21:46.908 --> 00:21:48.700
What the hell is happening?

00:23:20.866 --> 00:23:22.533
[PHOENIX]
Objection!

00:23:22.616 --> 00:23:24.616
The case of the stolen
Kurain urn has taken

00:23:24.700 --> 00:23:26.575
an unexpected turn.

00:23:26.658 --> 00:23:30.241
Ron was declared not guilty,
but now he's accused of murder!

00:23:30.325 --> 00:23:33.616
This must be a setup,
but who's behind it?

00:23:33.700 --> 00:23:36.241
And, after being
revealed as Mask DeMasque,

00:23:36.325 --> 00:23:38.283
the alliterative ace
Atmey's behavior

00:23:38.366 --> 00:23:39.908
has been troubling, too.

00:23:39.991 --> 00:23:42.116
Who's pulling the
strings in this case?

00:23:42.200 --> 00:23:45.241
Find the contradictions!
Believe in the truth!

00:23:45.325 --> 00:23:48.241
Next Episode: "The Stolen
Turnabout -- 3rd Trial"!

00:23:48.325 --> 00:23:49.325
Take that!
